add('electron-ohos-renderer-subprocess-main-proxy','Run renderer subprocess calls from the OH Electron main process','process',['electron'],
 'If a renderer cannot execute a packaged tool, replace its child_process with an IPC proxy and spawn in the main process, streaming stdio and exit back.',
 'execFile or spawn from a renderer reports ENOENT for a tool in a private HNP, though the same path runs from the main process.',
 'Electron OH apps with node integration whose renderer libraries spawn tools. Source comment attributes this to the render sandbox not seeing the HNP directory. A cross-process design has a security surface of its own, so limit it to known executables.',
 'renderer spawn ENOENT|child_process|execFile|HNP|ipcMain|webpack loader|NormalModuleReplacementPlugin|dugite|render sandbox',
 ['electron-ohos-non-pty-exec','electron-ohos-private-hnp','electron-ohos-process-isolation'],
 ['Confirm with a test: spawn the same absolute path from main and renderer.',
  'In the renderer bundle, swap the library\'s require of child_process with a webpack loader, as NormalModuleReplacementPlugin does not apply to a Node builtin.',
  'Implement spawn in main behind ipcMain, sending stdout, stderr and exit events per request ID and accepting stdin writes.',
  'Kill children when the sender fires destroyed, and restrict what can be launched to your packaged tools.',
  'Fill missing variables such as HOME, PATH and CA paths from main\'s environment. Replace cwd only where it is a neutral bundle location, so a really missing repository still returns ENOENT.'],
 'If you control the code, move the work into main or a utility service and call it explicitly, which is cleaner than emulating child_process. The source reports clone, commit and push on a device in its changelog.',
 'Exposing a general-purpose spawn to page content. Mapping every missing cwd to a safe path, which hides real errors. Leaving children alive after window destruction.',
 'From the renderer run success, non-zero exit, a missing cwd, large stdout, stdin input and a window closed mid-run. Confirm results match desktop and no process remains.',
 [('github-desktop-ohos',GP)],reports=['The source changelog reports device git operations; not repeated here.'])
add('hnp-tool-private-prefix-environment','Point a relocated tool at its private HNP install prefix','process',[],
 'Tools built with one install prefix cannot find helpers, configuration or CA files after private HNP installation, so set their locating variables in every process before the first spawn.',
 'A prebuilt tool in a private HNP starts but misses its helpers, configuration or CA file, for example git failing on sub-commands or TLS verification.',
 'OH apps that package command-line tools as private HNPs, installed under a /data/app/<name>.org/<name>_<version> path per the reviewed code. Git variables are the worked example; the approach applies to any relocatable tool with environment overrides.',
 'HNP|private install|GIT_EXEC_PATH|LOCAL_GIT_DIRECTORY|GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM|GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL|GIT_SSL_CAINFO|prefix|hnp.json',
 ['electron-ohos-private-hnp','native-curl-explicit-ca-bundle','hap-executable-declaration'],
 ['Find the actual install directory on a device and compare it with the prefix compiled into the tool.',
  'Derive paths from one constant kept in sync with hnp.json name and version, or read them at build time.',
  'Set the tool\'s overrides. For git: LOCAL_GIT_DIRECTORY, GIT_EXEC_PATH, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 and GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL pointing at an existing file you own.',
  'Set the CA path (GIT_SSL_CAINFO) from a bundled PEM, and prepend the HNP bin directories to PATH.',
  'Apply this in each process that spawns tools: renderers do not inherit changes made in main after they start.'],
 'Building the tool with a matching or relative prefix removes most of this, if the toolchain permits it. The compiled-in global config location in the reviewed git build was unreadable, which is why the explicit global file is needed.',
 'Letting version strings drift between hnp.json and code. Setting the environment in main only. Pointing GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL at a file that does not exist.',
 'From each process, run version, a sub-command that needs helpers, a config read and an HTTPS clone. Repeat after a version change.',
 [('github-desktop-ohos',GP),('github-desktop-ohos','hnp-src/ghdtools/hnp.json')])
add('ohos-git-ssh-sandbox-identity','Handle uid and passwd mismatch for git and ssh in the OH sandbox','process',[],
 'Tools relying on file ownership or passwd need explicit configuration: give ssh its files by option and give git a scoped safe.directory policy in an app-private config.',
 'git reports detected dubious ownership for repositories in user storage, and ssh ignores HOME, failing to find its config, known hosts or keys.',
 'Bundled git and OpenSSH in OH app processes. Per source comments, files in shared user storage (the currentUser directory) have a different uid from the app, and the app uid has no usable passwd entry. SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE depends on your OpenSSH version; the reviewed code relies on it with OpenSSH 9.8.',
 'dubious ownership|safe.directory|ssh HOME|passwd|GIT_SSH_COMMAND|UserKnownHostsFile|IdentityFile|SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE|currentUser storage',
 ['hnp-tool-private-prefix-environment','ohos-exec-helper-permission-section','sandbox-paths-and-app-identity'],
 ['Keep a global git config in app-private storage and refer to it with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL, so nothing leaks into other tools.',
  'Add safe.directory entries for repositories the user has selected. The reviewed code writes directory = *, which turns the ownership check off entirely; do that only with an understanding of the risk.',
  'Create ~/.ssh under the app home with an empty config, since ssh -F needs a file.',
  'Set GIT_SSH_COMMAND with -F, -o UserKnownHostsFile and -o IdentityFile to absolute paths, as ssh resolves ~ from passwd rather than HOME.',
  'Set SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE=force and SSH_ASKPASS to your prompt helper, with host-key confirmation handled through it.'],
 'The wildcard removes protection against malicious repositories with hooks or config in user storage. Selecting directories one by one is safer, at the cost of more prompts. Consider disabling repository hooks if you keep a wildcard.',
 'Setting safe.directory=* in a config other tools read. Assuming HOME controls ssh. Never persisting known_hosts, so every connection re-prompts.',
 'Open a repository in user storage, clone and push over SSH with a key and with a password, then with an unknown host and a changed host key.',
 [('github-desktop-ohos',GP)])
