add('electron-ohos-execpath-appspawn-fork','Check child_process.fork on OH Electron, where execPath can be appspawn','process',['electron'],
 'Test fork on your host before relying on it, since one reviewed host reports process.execPath as /system/bin/appspawn and fork fails with EACCES. No verified fix is known.',
 'child_process.fork fails with spawn /system/bin/appspawn EACCES, breaking process pools, plugin hosts or cluster workers.',
 'Observed on one Electron 37.2.0 OH port. Another source reports fork working on Electron 34 with ALLOW_WRITABLE_CODE_MEMORY, so this is host-scoped and the two reports are not reconciled. That permission concerns JIT memory, whereas this failure occurs at spawn.',
 'child_process.fork|execPath|appspawn|EACCES|cluster|plugin host|no-cluster|utilityProcess',
 ['electron-ohos-process-isolation','hap-executable-declaration','jit-executable-memory-authorization'],
 ['Log process.execPath at startup and run a small fork probe on the target device and runtime.',
  'If fork fails, run the workload in-process as a stopgap, such as a --no-cluster mode, accepting the loss of isolation.',
  'Evaluate alternatives on your runtime: a different process API, or a signed executable passed as execPath. The last is an untested curator suggestion, not an observed fix.',
  'Report which features degrade when a child process host is unavailable, rather than failing silently.'],
 'Unresolved: the reviewed port did not fix this and left its plugin host unadapted. Do not treat the permission from the other report as a fix without testing it.',
 'Inferring that fork works from a run on another runtime. Assuming the JIT permission addresses a spawn EACCES.',
 'Run the probe on each target host and record execPath, the runtime version, permissions declared and the result.',
 [('theia-ohos',TM),('theia-ohos','ohos-pc/evidence/theia-ohos-device.log'),('electron-harmonyos-kb','problems/fork-crash-missing-jit-permission.md')],status='unresolved')
